\begin{abstract}
% The phenomenal increase of mobile data traffic has been putting more and more significant pressure on the heterogeneous network (HetNet) in the past decade.
The device-to-device (D2D) communication underlaying a heterogeneous network (HetNet) has been suggested as an architecture of great potential in 5G network, particularly for the proximity-based applications such as device terminal relaying.
 These D2D user equipments (DUEs) may cause strong interference to nearby users, thus the interference management of which is an appealing topic.
 In this paper, we address the optimal time reuse for the HetNet with D2D relays and the corresponding user association scheme.
Due to the binary constraints of user association and the exponentially increasing number of reuse patterns, the problem turns to be a large scale integer programming that is formidable to solve.
A semi-distributed algorithm is proposed to solve this problem approximately.
Numerical simulations show our scheme can efficiently allocate the time resource
and offers significant gain relative to those conventional schemes.
\end{abstract}


\begin{IEEEkeywords}
Heterogeneous network, device-to-device (D2D) relays, time reuse, user association,
resource allocation
\end{IEEEkeywords}


\section{Introduction}
With the ever-increasing high-data-rate mobile traffic demands, the proximity-based communication through device-to-device (D2D) links is regarded as one promising technology in 5G cellular networks \cite{2014_survey}. 
D2D communication can significantly enhance network performance such as spectral and energy efficiencies \cite{2016_Xu_D2D} since it appears in short-range scenarios usually.
However, in one HetNet with D2D communications, the base station (BS)-based and the direct D2D links are coordinated to operate on the same licensed resource, which may cause severe interference without an efficient resource allocation strategy \cite{2017_Liu_interference}.
It is thus significant to investigate efficient resource management problems for D2D networks.

To make full use of the limited resource, a lot works have been done to optimize the mode selection, relay strategies and resource allocation in D2D underlaying cellular networks \cite{2015_Ye_distributed,2013_Xu_Cooperation,2016_Ma_HenNet_D2D,2016_Tang_MixMode,2016_Li_RB_allocation,2014_Ye_analysis,2013_Zhou_D2D_relay,2016_Mastronarde_D2D_relay,2015_Li_MMM}.
The D2D communications were considered to share the under-utilized uplink (UL) resource with BSs in recent works \cite{2015_Ye_distributed,2013_Xu_Cooperation,2016_Li_RB_allocation}.
However, interferences are more stronger in downlink (DL) cases, where D2D user equipments (DUEs) not only cause severe interference to nearby co-channel users, but also are strongly interfered by BSs \cite{2015_Ye_distributed}.
Additionally, nearly all the commercial user equipments are able to receive DL waveforms instead of the UL ones, which indicates that sharing DL resource possesses higher compatibility than UL.  
What's more, in the particular D2D relay cases, DL transmissions from BSs to DUEs will be likely to outweigh UL transmissions \cite{2015_Li_MMM}.
Therefore, it is more urgent to manage DL interference for D2D relays, such works were addressed in \cite{2016_Mastronarde_D2D_relay,2013_Zhou_D2D_relay,2015_Li_MMM}.
The D2D relays in \cite{2013_Zhou_D2D_relay} and \cite{2015_Li_MMM} were assumed to use orthogonal time or spectrum alternatively.
The authors in \cite{2016_Mastronarde_D2D_relay} modeled the inter-cell interference and minimized the power consumption for each DUE, while the interference between D2D relays were ignored.
Recently, spectrum reuse patterns were optimized for HetNets in \cite{2015_Zhuang,2016_Zhuang,2016_Kuang}.
They optimized over the average packet delay \cite{2015_Zhuang}, energy efficiency \cite{2016_Zhuang} and proportional fairness (PF) \cite{2016_Kuang} of a network 
% by considering total possible spectrum reuse patterns firstly.
through allocating resources to different spectrum reuse patterns.
The reuse patterns could also be regarded as a model to describe the interference in HetNets with D2D relays.

D2D communications are regarded as efficient methods for proximity-based service such as device terminal
relaying.
In this paper, the optimal set of time reuse patterns among the DUEs and
conventional BSs is studied to maximize the PF of the network. 
We put forward one efficient algorithm to solve the problem approximately in semi-distributed way. 
Our scheme can efficiently allocate transmission time to each server and offer significant gains relative to those conventional schemes.

The rest of this paper is organized as follows:
Section \ref{System_model} describes the system model.
Section \ref{Formulation} gives the problem formulation and characterizes the optimal time reuse profile.
In Section \ref{Algorithms}, the semi-distributed algorithm is proposed.
Numerical simulations are shown in Section \ref{Simulation} and Section \ref{Conclusion} concludes the paper.

